# Ask a live camera-mounted VLM detector (e.g. LocateAnything) whether an
# object is visible in the CURRENT frame, on demand.
#
# Called by the reasoner's read-only `locate_in_view` tool dispatch
# (openral_reasoner_ros.reasoner_node._dispatch_locate_in_view). The detector
# node (openral_perception_ros.ros_image_detector_node) runs a one-shot
# open-vocabulary detection on the latest frame of the requested camera and
# returns whether the queried object is in view. Read-only: no actuation.
#
# Request:
#   query    — free-text / label naming the object to look for (e.g. "red mug").
#              Sent verbatim as the detector's open-vocabulary query.
#   camera   — optional camera selector. Empty = the detector's primary/default
#              camera; otherwise one of the detector's configured camera ids so
#              the reasoner can choose a viewpoint. NOT a hardcoded name.
#   detector — optional on-demand locator selector (rSkill id / short alias,
#              e.g. "omdet-turbo-locator" or "locateanything-3b"). Empty = the
#              deployment's default locator. Routed to
#              /openral/perception/<detector>/locate_in_view; per-detector
#              namespacing lets several locators co-exist. Informational on the
#              server side (each node owns one model); echoed back so the
#              prompt cascade records which locator answered.
#   source_stamp_ns — optional source image timestamp. Zero means the latest
#                     available frame (the reasoner tool's default); nonzero
#                     requires that exact camera frame.
#
# Response:
#   found          — true iff the detector grounded the object in the frame.
#                    false with an empty `failure_reason` means inference ran
#                    successfully and found no match; false with a reason means
#                    visibility is unknown because the check did not complete.
#   camera         — the camera id actually queried (echoes the resolved default).
#   detector       — the locator id that answered (echoes the request, or the
#                    node's own id when the request left it empty).
#   source_stamp_ns — actual image source timestamp used; zero when no image was
#                     selected. A nonzero request is never answered from another
#                     frame.
#   metadata_json  — ObjectsMetadata JSON (boxes/labels/confidence) when found;
#                    empty when not found or the query could not complete; inspect
#                    `failure_reason` to distinguish a valid no-match from failure.
#   failure_reason — bounded cause when inference could not complete (for example
#                    `detector_inactive`, `no_frame`, or `detector_exception:…`).
#                    Empty only when inference completed successfully, including a
#                    successful no-match result.
#
#   roi_norm_xyxy — optional region of interest (x0, y0, x1, y1) in [0, 1] of the
#                   frame: the detector runs on that crop and answers in full-frame
#                   pixels. Empty = the whole frame (issue #418: the object tracker
#                   crops to its projected search region).
#   min_score     — optional detection floor for this call; 0 = the detector's own
#                   threshold (issue #418: a tracker prompt box is filtered downstream).

string query
string camera
string detector
int64 source_stamp_ns
float64[] roi_norm_xyxy
float32 min_score
---
bool found
string camera
string detector
int64 source_stamp_ns
string metadata_json
string<=128 failure_reason
